type: software
title: "Which central elements are transitive? An answer to a question of Campion Loth and Rattan on Jucys-Murphy evaluations"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. Symmetric polynomials in the Jucys-Murphy elements give the centre of the symmetric group algebra. Keeping only transitive products of transpositions defines the transitive image T_n(f), which Campion Loth and Rattan showed is central; they asked which subalgebra these images generate (Question 12). Over the complex numbers every central element is a single transitive image. Over a commutative ring R, transitive images span the centre, and generate it as a unital algebra, exactly when (n-1)! is a unit in R; when they span it, degree 2n-2 suffices and cannot be lowered. The pairs (ordinary evaluation, transitive image) are exactly the pairs of central elements with equal n-cycle coefficients. Over the integers a conjugation-orbit bound is attained classwise for n <= 5 and n = 7 but not for n = 6 (index 2), by exact computation."
